message.content:
{
  "summary": "Action potential propagation relies on local ion currents regenerating voltage patterns rather than transporting a single packet of ions. In unmyelinated axons, neighboring regions sequentially regenerate the signal, whereas myelinated axons utilize insulating myelin to concentrate regeneration at nodes of Ranvier, enabling saltatory conduction. This mechanism distinguishes short-distance charge movement from long-distance information propagation.",
  "topics": [
    "Mechanism of action potential propagation via local ion currents",
    "Signal regeneration in unmyelinated axons",
    "Structure and function of myelinated axons (nodes of Ranvier)",
    "Saltatory conduction as a specialized propagation method"
  ]
}

