  "summary": "Myelin production by specific glial cells (oligodendrocytes in the CNS, Schwann cells in the PNS) supports neuronal conduction but also involves broader regulatory functions by other glia like astrocytes. The functional integrity of neural circuits depends on both neurons and glia; structural damage to myelin can impair conduction even if the axon remains intact, illustrating that structural preservation does not guarantee normal physiological behavior.",
